IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 (2020 Revised Edition),
-- Singapore Statutes Online, current version as at 30 Sep 2026.
-- Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt (extracted from source/CPFTA2003.pdf).
--
-- The shared nouns, and nothing else: DECLARE only, no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Every other module imports this one.
--
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this
-- fact, or does answering it require reading the Act?  Only the first kind is
-- a field here.  "The supplier provides goods to consumers" is a fact.  "The
-- person is a supplier" is a rule, and is decided in cpfta-part1.l4.
--
-- Facts the Act takes from other Acts (whether a contract is a contract of sale
-- of goods within the Sale of Goods Act 1979; whether a person deals as consumer
-- under the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977; what a relevant contract is under the
-- Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984) are fields here too, because the answer
-- belongs to those Acts and is not encoded.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary: the nouns of section 2`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'supplier'"
DECLARE `Supplier Facts` HAS
    `the person acts in the course of the person's business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person provides goods or services to consumers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person manufactures, assembles or produces goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person promotes the use or purchase of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person receives or is entitled to receive money or other consideration as a result of the provision of goods or services to consumers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an employee or agent of a person who acts in the course of business and does any of those things` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'consumer' and s 2(2)"
DECLARE `Consumer Facts` HAS
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person acts exclusively in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person holds himself or herself out as acting exclusively in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person receives or has the right to receive goods or services from a supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has a legal obligation to pay a supplier for goods or services that have been or are to be supplied to another individual` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'financial product', 'financial services' and s 2(3)"
DECLARE `Regulated Thing Facts` HAS
    `the thing is regulated, or supplied by a person regulated, under a written law administered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is regulated, or supplied by a person regulated, under the Commodity Trading Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is regulated, or supplied by a person regulated, under another written law that the Minister has by order prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person supplying the thing is exempted from being licensed, approved or regulated under such a written law` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'residential property'"
DECLARE `Residential Property Facts` HAS
    `the thing is a house, flat or other premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is permitted by a written law to be used as a dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is in the course of being constructed` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'voucher'"
DECLARE `Voucher Facts` HAS
    `the thing is a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document purports to give the holder the right to obtain goods or a service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document purports to give the holder the right to obtain goods or a service at a discounted or reduced price` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'goods'"
DECLARE `Goods Facts` HAS
    `the thing is personal property, whether tangible or intangible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is a chattel attached or intended to be attached to real property on or after delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is credit, including credit extended solely on the security of land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation of the thing` IS A `Regulated Thing Facts`
    `residential property facts` IS A `Residential Property Facts`
    `voucher facts` IS A `Voucher Facts`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'time share contract', 'time share rights'"
DECLARE `Time Share Facts` HAS
    `the contract confers or purports to confer on an individual rights to use living accommodation used or intended to be used for leisure by a class of persons all of whom have such rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights are for a specified or ascertainable period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights arise under a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rights arise under an insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period during which the rights are exercisable, in years` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'services'"
DECLARE `Services Facts` HAS
    `the service involves the addition to or maintenance, repair or alteration of goods or residential property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the service is a membership in a club or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the club or organisation is a business formed to make a profit for its owners` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the service is the right to use time share accommodation under a time share contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `time share contract` IS A `Time Share Facts`
    `the service is a financial service` IS A `Regulated Thing Facts`
    `the service is offered or provided as financial services` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 2(1) 'consumer transaction'; First Schedule"
DECLARE `Transaction Facts` HAS
    `a supplier supplies goods or services to a consumer as a result of a purchase, lease, gift, contest or other arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a supplier and a consumer have an agreement, made as a result of a purchase, lease, gift, contest or other arrangement, under which the supplier is to supply goods or services to the consumer or to another consumer specified in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is a lease of residential property granted in consideration of rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is a time share contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is service provided under a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 2 -- Unfair practices: the nouns of sections 3 to 5`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 3"
DECLARE `Application Facts` HAS
    `the supplier is resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer is resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offer relating to the consumer transaction is made in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offer relating to the consumer transaction is sent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acceptance relating to the consumer transaction is made in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acceptance relating to the consumer transaction is sent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 5(3)(b)"
DECLARE `Attribution Facts` HAS
    `the act or omission is that of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee acted in the course of the employee's employment with the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act or omission is that of an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent was exercising powers or performing duties on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent acted within the scope of the agent's actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The Second Schedule, Part 1: one constructor per paragraph.
-- A representation is a statement or conduct by the supplier; the field
-- `the representation is accurate` records whether what was represented is in fact so.

DECLARE Representation HAS
    `the representation is made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the representation is accurate` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 1"
DECLARE `Second Schedule Practice` IS ONE OF
    `Paragraph 1` HAS
        `1 characteristics represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 2` HAS
        `2 supplier's sponsorship, approval or affiliation represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 3` HAS
        `3 the need for goods or services represented` IS A Representation
        `3 the representation is false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 4` HAS
        `4 standard, quality, grade, style, model, origin, weight, volume, length, capacity or method of manufacture represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 5` HAS
        `5 goods represented as new or unused` IS A Representation
        `5 the goods have deteriorated or been altered, reconditioned or reclaimed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 6` HAS
        `6 use, extent of use, history or particular use of goods represented` IS A Representation
        `6 the supplier knows it is not so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 7` HAS
        `7 availability, or reason, price, quantity or time of availability represented` IS A Representation
        `7 the supplier knows or can reasonably be expected to know it is not so` IS A BOOLEAN
        `7 the representation clearly states any limitation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 8` HAS
        `8 need or desirability of a service, part, repair or replacement, or that one has been supplied, installed, made or provided, represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 9` HAS
        `9 existence of a price benefit or advantage represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 10` HAS
        `10 the supplier provided an estimate to the consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
        `10 the supplier charges a price substantially higher than the estimate` IS A BOOLEAN
        `10 the consumer expressly agreed to the higher price in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 11` HAS
        `11 rights, remedies or obligations in a transaction represented` IS A Representation
        `11 the representation is deceptive or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 12` HAS
        `12 authority to negotiate the final terms of an agreement represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 13` HAS
        `13 the supplier includes terms or conditions in an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
        `13 the terms or conditions are harsh, oppressive or excessively one-sided` IS A BOOLEAN
        `13 the terms or conditions are so unconscionable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 14` HAS
        `14 the supplier exerts undue pressure or undue influence on the consumer to enter into a transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 15` HAS
        `15 the supplier represents that another supplier will, on presentment of a voucher, supply certain goods or services, or supply them at a discounted or reduced price` IS A BOOLEAN
        `15 the supplier knows or ought to know that on presentment they will not be supplied, or not at a discounted or reduced price` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 16` HAS
        `16 the supplier makes a representation that appears in an objective form such as an editorial, documentary or scientific report` IS A BOOLEAN
        `16 the representation is primarily made to sell goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `16 the representation states that it is an advertisement or a promotion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 17` HAS
        `17 the supplier represents that a particular person has offered or agreed to acquire goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `17 the person has in fact offered or agreed to acquire them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 18` HAS
        `18 availability of facilities for repair of goods or of spare parts represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 19` HAS
        `19 the supplier offers gifts, prizes or other free items in connection with the supply of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `19 the supplier knows or ought to know that the items will not be provided or provided as offered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 20` HAS
        `20 the supplier represents that goods or services are available at a discounted price for a stated period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
        `20 the supplier knows or ought to know that they will continue to be so available for a substantially longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 21` HAS
        `21 the particular reason for a discounted price represented` IS A Representation
    `Paragraph 22` HAS
        `22 the supplier invites a consumer to purchase, or offers to sell, original goods or services at a certain price` IS A BOOLEAN
        `22 the supplier acts with the intention of promoting different goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `22 the supplier refuses to show or demonstrate the original goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `22 the supplier refuses to take any order for the original goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `22 the supplier refuses to supply the original goods or services in a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
        `22 the supplier shows or demonstrates a defective sample of the original goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 23` HAS
        `23 the supplier omits to provide a material fact to a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
        `23 the supplier uses small print to conceal a material fact from the consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
        `23 the supplier misleads a consumer as to a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
        `23 the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the information would affect the decision of a consumer to enter into a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
        `23 the supplier does so in connection with the supply of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 24` HAS
        `24 the supplier accepts payment or other consideration for the supply of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `24 a period for supply was specified at or before the time the payment or consideration was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
        `24 the supplier knows or ought to know that it will not be able to supply within the specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
        `24 the supplier knows or ought to know that it will not be able to supply within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 25` HAS
        `25 the supplier purports to assert a right to payment for the supply of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `25 the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 26` HAS
        `26 the supplier sends the consumer an invoice or document that states the amount of payment for the supply of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `26 the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
        `26 the most prominent text of the document is "This is not a bill. You are not required to pay any money." or words to that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
        `26 the consumer has expressly acknowledged to the supplier in writing the consumer's intention to accept and pay for the goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Paragraph 27` HAS
        `27 an applicable agreement has been entered into in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
        `27 a copy of the applicable agreement has not been given to the consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
        `27 the consumer has requested a copy of the applicable agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
        `27 the supplier refuses to give the consumer a copy of the applicable agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraphs 1 and 2"
DECLARE `Unsolicited Facts` HAS
    `the goods or services are supplied in relation to a consumer transaction to a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer requested the goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only ground for finding a request is one of payment, use, dealing or disposal, a request to purchase another similar good or service, or inaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer knows or ought to have known that the goods or services were intended for delivery to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was reasonable to believe that the goods or services, if delivered to that other person, would have been unsolicited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods or services are supplied on a continuing basis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a material change in the goods or services, or in their supply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer consented in writing to the material change` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only ground for finding consent to the material change is payment, use, dealing or disposal, a request to purchase another similar good or service, or inaction` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 3"
DECLARE `Applicable Agreement Facts` HAS
    `the agreement is between a supplier and a consumer for the supply of goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement expressly provides that the goods or services will not be supplied, or begin to be supplied, until the price or part of the price has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement expressly provides that the price is to be paid by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of instalments, not counting any deposit` IS A NUMBER
    `the consumer has paid a deposit` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 4"
DECLARE `Unfair Practice Facts` HAS
    `the supplier acts in relation to a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier does or says something, or omits to do or say something` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as a result a consumer might reasonably be deceived or misled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier makes a false claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier takes advantage of a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the consumer is not in a position to protect his or her own interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the consumer is not reasonably able to understand the character, nature, language or effect of the transaction or any matter related to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the practices specified in the Second Schedule that the supplier engages in` IS A LIST OF `Second Schedule Practice`

§ `Part 2 -- Unfair practices: the nouns of sections 6 to 12 and the Fifth Schedule`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(4)"
DECLARE `Residential Valuation Facts` HAS
    `the annual value of the immovable property appearing in the Valuation List prepared under section 10 of the Property Tax Act 1960` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the annual rent payable by the tenant in respect of the immovable property` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the monthly rent payable by the tenant in respect of the immovable property` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the last transacted price` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(1) to (6)"
DECLARE `Consumer Action Facts` HAS
    `the consumer has entered a consumer transaction involving an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is commenced in a court of competent jurisdiction against the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is a claim for money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of the claim` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount claimed is a balance after a set-off admitted by the consumer in the particulars of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the balance after that set-off` IS A NUMBER
    `the subject matter is residential property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the subject matter, where it is not residential property` IS A NUMBER
    `the valuation facts of the residential property` IS A `Residential Valuation Facts`
    `the consumer has abandoned the excess over the prescribed limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the limit prescribed by the Minister by order in the Gazette in place of $30,000` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 6(7) to (9)"
DECLARE `Stay Facts` HAS
    `a party to the action applies for a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an application has been made under section 9 against the same supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings relate to the unfair practice to which the application relates` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied that the determination of the application under section 9 will be material to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the stay order was made on` IS A DATE
    `the date of the last further step taken by any party after the stay order` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date on which the court considers discontinuing the proceedings` IS A DATE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Kind of Action` IS ONE OF
    `an action under section 6(1)`
    `an action under section 8(6), (7) or (8)`
    `an action under regulations made under section 11`
    `an action under provisions specified under section 43(2)(j)`
    `an action relating to a deposit paid in relation to or in contemplation of a motor vehicle sale contract`
    `any other action`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Tribunal Jurisdiction Facts` HAS
    `kind of action` IS A `Kind of Action`
    `the action relates to an unfair practice or an undertaking in respect of an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract is a contract mentioned in paragraph 1(a) or (c) of the Schedule to the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract relates to the sale of immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action relates to a time share contract or a time share related contract` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of Relief` IS ONE OF
    `restitution of money, property or other consideration given or furnished by the consumer`
    `damages in the amount of any loss or damage suffered by the consumer`
    `specific performance against the supplier`
    `an order to repair goods or provide parts for goods`
    `an order varying the contract between the supplier and the consumer`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(5) to (9)"
DECLARE `Relief Facts` HAS
    `the court is a Small Claims Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court finds that the supplier has engaged in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is an action under section 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer intends to resell the goods or services in the course of the consumer's business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer intends to use up or transform the goods in the course of the consumer's business in a process of production or manufacturing or in repairing or treating other goods or fixtures` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods or services are otherwise intended for business use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the share of the goods or services attributed by the court to non-business use, where it has apportioned the use` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 7(10) and (11)"
DECLARE `Regard Facts` HAS
    `the court finds that an unfair practice has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is making an order in an action under section 6(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a specified dispute resolution scheme was available to the consumer in respect of the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(3)"
DECLARE `Kind of Undertaking` IS ONE OF
    `an undertaking that the supplier will not engage in the unfair practice`
    `an undertaking to compensate a consumer who has suffered loss or damage as a result of an unfair practice`
    `an undertaking to reimburse a specified body for costs or expenses incurred by it`
    `an undertaking to publicise the voluntary compliance agreement`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(1) to (5)"
DECLARE Undertaking HAS
    `kind` IS A `Kind of Undertaking`
    `the supplier agrees to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is included in or varied in the agreement at the request of the consumer to whom it relates` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(1) to (5), (10), (11)"
DECLARE `Voluntary Compliance Agreement Facts` HAS
    `the body inviting the supplier is a person or body appointed by the Minister as a specified body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appointment has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the supplier has engaged, is engaging or is likely to engage in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the undertakings in the agreement` IS A LIST OF Undertaking

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 8(6) to (9) and s 12(2)"
DECLARE `Undertaking Enforcement Facts` HAS
    `the undertaking enforced` IS A `Kind of Undertaking`
    `the supplier has failed to comply with the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of the failure to comply` IS A DATE
    `the date on which the action is commenced` IS A DATE
    `recovery under the agreement or under section 8(6), (7) or (8) has already been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement provides otherwise as to the bar on further actions` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of Court` IS ONE OF
    `the District Court`
    `the General Division of the High Court`
    `any other court`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(1) to (3)"
DECLARE `Declaration Application Facts` HAS
    `the applicant is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court` IS A `Kind of Court`
    `the supplier has engaged, is engaging or is likely to engage in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied that the supplier has engaged in the unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied that, if a declaration or an injunction is not granted, it is likely that the supplier will engage in the unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application for an injunction is pending determination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court considers an interim injunction desirable` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(4) and Fifth Schedule"
DECLARE `Notifiable Event` IS ONE OF
    `the individual, as a sole proprietor, commences carrying on business as a supplier`
    `the individual is employed or ceases to be employed by a person who carries on a business as a supplier`
    `the individual becomes or ceases to be a director of a company which carries on a business as a supplier`
    `the individual becomes or ceases to be a partner in a partnership or limited partnership which carries on a business as a supplier`
    `the individual becomes or ceases to be a partner or manager of a limited liability partnership which carries on a business as a supplier`
    `the individual becomes or ceases to be interested in voting power or issued shares in a company which carries on a business as a supplier` HAS
        `the percentage of the total voting power or of the total issued shares, whichever is greater` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(4)(d)"
DECLARE `Business Change Event` IS ONE OF
    `a change in the premises or number of premises at which the supplier carries on business as a supplier`
    `a change in the Internet address or number of Internet addresses through which consumer transactions with the supplier may be entered into`
    `the supplier converts from a firm or private company to a limited liability partnership`
    `the supplier undergoes an arrangement, reconstruction or amalgamation under Part 7 of the Companies Act 1967`
    `an order is made under section 71 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 approving a compromise or an arrangement`
    `the supplier is subject to receivership under Part 6 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `the supplier is subject to judicial management under Parts 7 and 9 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `the supplier is subject to winding up under Parts 8 and 9 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `another event prescribed under the Act`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(4)"
DECLARE `Accompanying Order` IS ONE OF
    `an order to publish periodically, at the supplier's expense, the details of the declaration or injunction`
    `an order to notify each consumer in writing and obtain the consumer's written acknowledgment before a contract is entered into`
    `an order to include in every invoice or receipt a statement that a declaration or injunction has been granted`
    `an order to notify the Commission in writing within 14 days after a business change event` HAS
        `the event` IS A `Business Change Event`
    `an order that an individual supplier inform the Commission in writing if a notifiable event occurs`
    `an order that one or all of the individual partners of a partnership inform the Commission in writing if a notifiable event occurs`
    `an order to reimburse the Commission for the cost of publishing notices`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(6) to (11)"
DECLARE `Order Period Facts` HAS
    `the accompanying orders made against the supplier` IS A LIST OF `Accompanying Order`
    `the periods specified for the orders mentioned in section 9(4)(a), (b), (c) and (d), in years` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `the period specified for an order mentioned in section 9(4)(e) or (f), in years` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 10 years` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the supplier or individual has failed to comply with an order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aggregate in years of the specified period and all extensions` IS A NUMBER
    `the Commission applies for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(12)"
DECLARE `Cancellation Facts` HAS
    `the supplier entered into a consumer transaction in breach of an accompanying order to notify the consumer and obtain acknowledgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the contract was entered into` IS A DATE
    `the date on which the consumer cancels` IS A DATE

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 9(14)"
DECLARE `Conclusive Proof Facts` HAS
    `the practice has been declared or permanently enjoined by the District Court or the General Division of the High Court as an unfair practice under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are civil proceedings involving the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are an appeal from the order` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 10"
DECLARE `Abettor Injunction Facts` HAS
    `the applicant is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court` IS A `Kind of Court`
    `the court is satisfied that the person has knowingly abetted, aided, permitted or procured the supplier to engage in the unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied that, if an injunction is not granted, it is likely that the person will knowingly abet, aid, permit or procure the supplier to engage in the unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court considers an interim injunction desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the specified period in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the period in years that the Minister has prescribed in place of 5 years` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 12(1), (6) to (8) and Fourth Schedule"
DECLARE `Consumer Knowledge Facts` HAS
    `the date on which the consumer actually had knowledge of the unfair practice` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date on which the consumer might reasonably have been expected to acquire knowledge from facts observable or ascertainable by the consumer` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date on which the consumer might reasonably have been expected to acquire knowledge from facts ascertainable with appropriate expert advice which it is reasonable to seek` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the consumer has taken all reasonable steps to obtain, and where appropriate to act on, that expert advice` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of Limited Action` IS ONE OF
    `an action under section 6`
    `an action under section 8(6), (7) or (8)`
    `an action under section 9`
    `an action under section 10`
    `an action under regulations made under section 11`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 12 and Fourth Schedule"
DECLARE `Limitation Facts` HAS
    `kind of action` IS A `Kind of Limited Action`
    `the date on which the action is commenced` IS A DATE
    `the date of the occurrence of the last material event on which the action is based` IS A DATE
    `the date of the failure to comply with the undertaking` IS A DATE
    `the date of the cancellation of the contract` IS A DATE
    `the Commission alleges in the action an unfair practice in respect of a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `what the consumer knew` IS A `Consumer Knowledge Facts`
    `the person to whom the action accrued was under a disability on the date after which the period of limitation begins to run` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which that person ceased to be under a disability or died, whichever first occurred` IS A MAYBE DATE

§ `Part 3 -- Additional consumer rights in respect of non-conforming goods: the nouns of sections 13 to 18`

DECLARE `Kind of Applicable Contract` IS ONE OF
    `a contract of sale of goods`
    `a contract for the transfer of goods`
    `a hire-purchase agreement`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 13(3) and (4), s 14(1), (3), (4)"
DECLARE `Non-conforming Goods Facts` HAS
    `kind of contract` IS A `Kind of Applicable Contract`
    `the transferee deals as consumer under Part 1 of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferor claims that the transferee does not deal as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferor has shown that the transferee does not deal as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract was made on` IS A DATE
    `the goods were delivered on` IS A DATE
    `there is a breach of an express term of the contract in relation to the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a breach of a term implied by section 13, 14 or 15 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a breach of a term implied by section 3, 4 or 5 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a breach of a term implied by section 6A, 6B or 6C of the Hire-Purchase Act 1969` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lack of conformity is shown to have existed at the time of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the lack of conformity appeared` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `it is established that the goods did conform at the date of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applying the presumption is incompatible with the nature of the goods or the nature of the lack of conformity` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Remedy IS ONE OF
    Repair
    Replacement

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 15(3) and (4)"
DECLARE `Remedy Facts` HAS
    `the remedy is impossible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the remedy imposes on the transferor costs that are unreasonable in comparison with those imposed by the other remedy, taking into account the value the goods would have if they conformed, the significance of the lack of conformity and whether the other remedy could be effected without significant inconvenience` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the remedy imposes on the transferor costs that are unreasonable in comparison with those imposed by an appropriate reduction in the amount to be paid or by rescission, taking into account the same three matters` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, ss 15 to 17"
DECLARE `Remedy Claim Facts` HAS
    `the transferee requires the transferor to repair or replace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the remedy required` IS A Remedy
    `facts of repair` IS A `Remedy Facts`
    `facts of replacement` IS A `Remedy Facts`
    `the transferor repaired or replaced the goods within a reasonable time and without causing significant inconvenience to the transferee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee rejects the goods and terminates the contract for breach of condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee, having required repair or replacement, further requires the goods to be repaired or replaced by the other remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee has given the transferor a reasonable time in which to repair or replace` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 18"
DECLARE `Court Power Facts` HAS
    `proceedings in which a remedy is sought under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee applies for specific performance of an obligation imposed on the transferor by section 15` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee requires the transferor to give effect to a remedy under section 15 or 16, or claims to rescind under section 16` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court decides that another remedy under section 15 or 16 is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transferee has claimed to rescind the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tribunal is a Small Claims Tribunal acting within its jurisdiction under section 5 of the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 3A -- Investigation powers: the nouns of sections 19 to 26`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 19(1)"
DECLARE `Suspicion Facts` HAS
    `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a supplier has engaged, is engaging or is likely to engage in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person has knowingly abetted, aided, permitted or procured a supplier to engage in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that a person is knowingly abetting, aiding, permitting or procuring a supplier to engage in an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of Appointee` IS ONE OF
    `an officer or employee of the Commission`
    `an auxiliary police officer appointed under Part 9 of the Police Force Act 2004`
    `any other person`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 19(2) to (4)"
DECLARE `Officer Facts` HAS
    `the chief executive made the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `kind of appointee` IS A `Kind of Appointee`
    `the officer declared the officer's office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer, on demand, produced to the person affected the identification card the chief executive issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person refuses to comply with a request, demand or order of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 20"
DECLARE `Document Notice Facts` HAS
    `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is given to a supplier or person mentioned in section 19(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission considers the specified document, article or information relevant to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice indicates the purpose for which the document, article or information is required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is accompanied by a copy of the offences under sections 27, 28, 29 and 30` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 21(1) to (4)"
DECLARE `Entry Without Warrant Facts` HAS
    `the entry is in connection with an investigation under section 19(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are reasonably suspected of being used by the person under investigation in connection with an unfair practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the entrant is an investigation officer, or a person the Commission has authorised in writing to accompany and assist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the occupier was given a written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of working days' notice of the intended entry given in the notice` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice indicates the subject matter and purpose of the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is accompanied by a copy of the offences under sections 27, 28, 29 and 30` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the investigation officer has taken all the steps that are reasonably practicable to give notice but has not been able to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `evidence of the authorisation of the investigation officer and of every authorised assistant is produced` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a document containing the information about subject matter, purpose and the offences is produced` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Warrant Condition` IS ONE OF
    `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which have not been produced as required under section 20 or 21(5)(e)`
    `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents which the Commission may require under section 20, and that if required they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed`
    `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are on any premises documents or goods within section 21, and that if notice is given under section 21(2) they would be concealed, removed, tampered with or destroyed`
    `an investigation officer or authorised assistant has attempted to enter under section 21 but been unable to, and there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that there are documents or goods on the premises`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 22"
DECLARE `Warrant Facts` HAS
    `the applicant is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conditions established for the premises` IS A LIST OF `Warrant Condition`
    `the warrant names an investigation officer and one or more authorised assistants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the warrant indicates the subject matter and purpose of the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the warrant is accompanied by a copy of the offences under sections 27, 28, 29 and 30` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the warrant was issued` IS A DATE
    `the date on which the warrant is exercised` IS A DATE
    `the warrant was produced to the person against whom power is exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are unoccupied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the officer took reasonable steps to inform the occupier of the intended entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the occupier was informed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the occupier or the occupier's representative was given a reasonable opportunity to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy of the warrant was left in a prominent place on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises were left as effectively secured as they were found` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 23"
DECLARE `Seizure Facts` HAS
    `the seized item is a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person from whose possession the document was taken requested a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner of the goods, document or information was informed of the possession, seizure or detention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods were seized from a vending machine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proprietor named on the machine, or if none the occupier of the premises, was informed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods, document or information were placed in safe custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceedings under section 9 or 10 (including on appeal) are completed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods, document or information retained may be evidence in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 24 and s 25"
DECLARE `Examination Facts` HAS
    `the person is reasonably believed by an investigation officer to have engaged in an unfair practice or knowingly abetted, aided, permitted or procured a supplier to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person appears to be acquainted with facts or circumstances relevant to the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is within the limits of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement was read over to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person does not understand English` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement was interpreted in a language the person understands` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement was signed by the person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 26"
DECLARE `Disclosure Facts` HAS
    `the person is required under a provision of the Act to disclose information or a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person claims, before disclosing, that disclosure might tend to incriminate the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are proceedings under Part 3B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a professional legal adviser, or a legal counsel in an entity, acting in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information or document is or contains a privileged communication` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 3B -- Offences: the nouns of sections 27 to 34`

DECLARE `Kind of Offence` IS ONE OF
    `an offence of failing to comply with a requirement (section 27)`
    `an offence of destroying or falsifying documents (section 28)`
    `an offence of giving false or misleading information (section 29)`
    `an offence of obstructing an officer of the Commission (section 30)`

DECLARE `Penalty` HAS
    `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum term of imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 27"
DECLARE `Refusal Facts` HAS
    `the person fails to comply with a requirement imposed under section 20, 21, 22, 24 or 25` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement is to produce a document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document was in the person's possession or under the person's control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was reasonably practicable for the person to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement is to provide information, to provide an explanation of a document, or to state where a document is to be found` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person had a reasonable excuse for failing to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person imposing the requirement failed to act in accordance with the section under which it was imposed` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 28"
DECLARE `Destruction Facts` HAS
    `the person has been required to produce a document under section 20, 21, 22 or 24` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person intentionally or recklessly destroys, disposes of, falsifies or conceals the document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person causes or permits the destruction, disposal, falsification or concealment of the document` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 29"
DECLARE `False Information Facts` HAS
    `the person provides information to the Commission, an investigation officer or an authorised assistant in connection with an investigation under section 19(1) or an offence in Part 3B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person provides information to another person, knowing it is to be used to provide information to the Commission, an investigation officer or an authorised assistant in connection with a function or duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knows the information to be false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is reckless as to whether the information is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 30"
DECLARE `Obstruction Facts` HAS
    `the person obstructs, hinders or impedes a member, officer or employee of the Commission, or an investigation officer or authorised assistant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person does so in the discharge of duties or the exercise of powers under the Act or its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 31"
DECLARE `Seizure Proceedings Facts` HAS
    `the proceedings are before a court in respect of equipment, goods, an article or a document seized in the exercise or purported exercise of a power under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the relief sought is an order for the return of the item or the payment of its value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Kind of Body` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation, including a limited liability partnership`
    `an unincorporated association`
    `a partnership`

DECLARE `Role in Body` IS ONE OF
    `an officer of the corporation, unincorporated association or a member of its governing body`
    `a partner, or a person purporting to act as a partner`
    `an individual involved in the management of the body who is in a position to influence its conduct in relation to the commission of the offence`
    `none of those`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, ss 32(2) and 33(2)"
DECLARE `Body Offence Facts` HAS
    `kind of body` IS A `Kind of Body`
    `the body commits an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's role` IS A `Role in Body`
    `the person consented or connived, or conspired with others, to effect the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is in any other way, by act or omission, knowingly concerned in or party to the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person knew or ought reasonably to have known that the offence, or an offence of the same type, would be or is being committed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, ss 32(1) and 33(1)"
DECLARE `State of Mind Facts` HAS
    `it is necessary in a proceeding for an offence under the Act to prove the state of mind of the body in relation to particular conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an officer of the body engaged in that conduct within the scope of actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee of the body engaged in that conduct within the scope of actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an agent of the body engaged in that conduct within the scope of actual or apparent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that person had that state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 34"
DECLARE `Composition Facts` HAS
    `the offence is prescribed as a compoundable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person compounding is the chief executive or an officer of the Commission authorised by the chief executive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maximum fine prescribed for the offence` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum proposed to be collected` IS A NUMBER
    `the sum has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 4 -- General: the nouns of sections 35 to 44`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 35"
DECLARE `Contracting Out Facts` HAS
    `the term is contained in a contract, or is an agreement to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term is inconsistent with the provisions of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term is a waiver or release of a right, benefit or protection conferred under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the release was made by a person in settlement of a dispute` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 36"
DECLARE `Successor Facts` HAS
    `the individual is an heir or assignee of a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual receives goods or services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual receives them in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 38"
DECLARE `Publisher Facts` HAS
    `the person prints, publishes, distributes, broadcasts or telecasts an advertisement on behalf of a supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person does so in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person does so in the ordinary course of the person's business` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 39"
DECLARE `Parol Evidence Facts` HAS
    `the evidence is parol or extrinsic evidence establishing the existence of an express warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action relates to a consumer transaction between a consumer and a supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods or services are intended for business use` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 40"
DECLARE `Document Facts` HAS
    `a consumer and a supplier enter into a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all or part of the transaction or contract is evidenced by a document provided by the supplier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of the document is ambiguous` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 41"
DECLARE `Burden Facts` HAS
    `the proceedings are taken in a court between a consumer and a supplier in relation to a consumer transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a dispute arises as to whether the supplier has complied with a requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement is specified by regulations made under section 41(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 44"
DECLARE `Kind of Transitional Matter` IS ONE OF
    `proceedings for a declaration or an injunction under section 9 or 10`
    `an order of the District Court or the High Court under section 9 or 10 requiring a person to notify, inform, reimburse or do anything in relation to the Board`
    `an investigation under Part 3A`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 44"
DECLARE `Transitional Facts` HAS
    `kind of matter` IS A `Kind of Transitional Matter`
    `the matter was commenced or made by, or in relation to, the Standards, Productivity and Innovation Board` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on which it was commenced or made` IS A DATE
    `it is pending, or the order remains unsatisfied, on 2 April 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person notifies, informs, reimburses or does the thing in relation to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, ss 9(4)(d) to (f) and 10(6)(c)"
DECLARE `Party to an order` IS ONE OF
    `The supplier`
    `The individual`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, ss 9(4)(d) to (f) and 10(6)(c)"
DECLARE `Act under an order` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Commission in writing of a business change event` HAS
        `the business change event` IS A `Business Change Event`
    `inform the Commission in writing of a notifiable event` HAS
        `the notifiable event` IS A `Notifiable Event`
